invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: exponent_digit reads the low half of each byte before the high
  half, so the window raises the message to the exponent with the two
  digits of every byte exchanged. An exponent whose bytes each hold one
  digit twice, such as 0 or all ones, still gives the right power.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test runs the exponents 16 and 17, the top bit alone
  and random ones, and requires the ladder's bytes.

--- old
    return ((uint64_t)e[i >> 1] >> (WINDOW_BITS * (1 - (i & 1)))) & (TABLE_ENTRIES - 1);
--- new
    return ((uint64_t)e[i >> 1] >> (WINDOW_BITS * (i & 1))) & (TABLE_ENTRIES - 1);
